{
  "_comment": [
    "Spreadsheet header spellings and the canonical column name each",
    "normalises to. Shared with the Telar Compositor, which keeps its own",
    "copy and maintains the union: one vocabulary, two implementations,",
    "and until this existed no test on either side could see the other's.",
    "Three divergences were found by one side asking the other (the",
    "'medium' family, the manual-step audience values, and the accented",
    "aliases); this is the instrument that replaces asking.",
    "",
    "Generated from the framework's COLUMN_NAME_MAPPING and then owned by",
    "hand: regenerating it would only ever restate what this side already",
    "does, which is the half a shared fixture is not for.",
    "",
    "Gender is meaning, not spelling: 'privado' and 'privada' are separate",
    "entries on purpose. Accent variants may be derived; final vowels may",
    "never be."
  ],
